# eth_axi_xbar formal proof (SymbiYosys).
# Proves the per-destination lock-step discipline — regression guard for the
# 2026-09-01 cross-master same-destination B/R/W response-aliasing bug
# (report-E1-RUN3): (U) per-destination in-flight uniqueness, (C) busy<->
# in-flight consistency (wr_busy/rd_busy == the in-flight set), (O) B/R owner
# routing (a response routes ONLY to the master that issued the transaction),
# (B) v0.1 burst BOUNDING (E2-AXI2): the per-master beat counters never run
# past the AxLEN/ArLEN captured with the granted AW/AR, so a routed burst is
# exactly as long as its master asked for. The destination's busy bit is held
# for the WHOLE burst, so (U)/(C) hold mid-burst as well.
# plus AXI response VALID stability. Assumptions constrain the attached
# masters/slaves to the AXI handshake (incl. the v0.1 burst attributes
# AxLEN/AxSIZE/AxBURST/WLAST) + A3.4.1 response-ordering contracts.
# The cover task witnesses concurrent multi-master traffic (incl. the DECERR
# slave) and multi-beat bursts so the safety proof is non-vacuous. Liveness is
# out of scope for prove-mode k-induction (needs fairness) — see the FORMAL
# block in the RTL.
# Run:  sby -f eth_axi_xbar.sby
# Config: 2 masters x 2 slaves (+ DECERR slave); BURST_EN=1 (v0.1 burst path);
# ADDR_MAP: slave0 @ 0x000-xx, slave1 @ 0x100-xx (mask 0xFFFFFF00), everything
# else -> DECERR.
[tasks]
prove
cover

[options]
prove: mode prove
prove: depth 40
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 40

[engines]
prove: smtbmc
cover: smtbmc

[script]
read -formal eth_axi_skidbuf.sv
read -formal eth_axi_xbar.sv
chparam -set N_MST 2 -set N_SLV 2 -set BURST_EN 1 -set ADDR_MAP 128'hFFFFFF00FFFFFF000000010000000000 eth_axi_xbar
prep -top eth_axi_xbar

[files]
ethereal-shell/rtl/axi/eth_axi_skidbuf.sv
ethereal-shell/rtl/axi/eth_axi_xbar.sv
